abstract: >-
  Nexus-MCP is a unified, local-first MCP server that combines hybrid search
  (vector + BM25), a static code graph with call edges, and persistent
  semantic memory into a single process. It provides 8 tools for AI coding
  agents via the Model Context Protocol. The tools aim at fewer agent turns
  for the same answers. It uses about 90 MB of RAM idle and 460 MB with the
  embedding model loaded, needs no API keys and has no cloud dependencies.
